// REJECTS: Field 'points' is required
//
// `points` is REQUIRED on a propertyView, and this is the surprising one: an empty list is
// legal (`points: [];` appears in diagram-full.pure), so the field carries no information
// when omitted -- and is still mandatory.
//
// That combination is what a rewrite gets wrong. "Required" and "may be empty" look
// contradictory, so the natural implementation defaults a missing points to [] and moves
// on. It produces the identical protocol legend-engine would have produced from `points:
// [];` -- which is exactly why nothing downstream ever notices the file should not have
// loaded.
###Diagram
Diagram fixture::neg::NoPoints
{
   propertyView
   {
      property: fixture::neg::Person.firm;
      source: a;
      target: b;
   }
}
